    "title": "Lost 82-year-old woman found safe, thanks to her furry protector - NewsBreak",
    "text": "4 hours ago An 82-year-old resident of Elmira who went missing Monday, Dec. 29, was found late that night thanks to the help of her dog, Cami. Cami, a blue heeler, also known as an Australian cattle dog, has been known for her loyalty to her owner. This time, the pup went above and beyond, keeping the woman warm as temperatures dipped below freezing, according to a release from the Lane County Sheriff’s Office. The dog also “signaled to nearby Lane County Search and Rescue volunteers coming through the area,” the release said. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 6",
